# Cloudflare Pages header rules.
#
# Vite's bundles carry a content hash in their filename, so they are safe to
# cache hard. Anything the app fetches by a FIXED name is not: if such a file
# is later changed or removed, a long edge cache keeps serving the old copy
# long after the deploy.
#
# That is what split the deployed game from the local one. `assets/manifest.json`
# was deleted from the build, but Cloudflare went on serving it with
# `s-maxage=604800` - seven days - along with the placeholder sprites it named,
# so the deployed game loaded art the bundle no longer shipped. The build now
# decides whether baked art exists (see vite.config.ts), and this keeps the
# manifest itself revalidating for when real baked art does ship.
/assets/manifest.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
